<main id="top"><section class="public-hero"><span class="public-orb orb-one"></span><span class="public-orb orb-two"></span><span class="public-orb orb-three"></span><div class="public-container hero-content"><p class="public-kicker reveal-public">MSWDO TAGUDIN · ILOCOS SUR</p><h1 class="reveal-public">Assistance to Individuals in Crisis Situations <em>(AICS)</em></h1><p class="hero-lead reveal-public">Practical support for Tagudin residents facing difficult circumstances—from medical and burial needs to food, transportation, and education assistance.</p><a class="public-cta reveal-public" href="#avail">Learn How to Avail <span>↓</span></a><p class="hero-note reveal-public">Libre nga serbisyo para kadagiti kwalipikado a residente ti Tagudin.</p></div></section>
<section class="public-section" id="about"><div class="public-container two-col"><div class="section-intro observe"><p class="public-kicker">ABOUT THE PROGRAM</p><h2>Help when it matters most.</h2><p>AICS is a government assistance program administered by the Municipal Social Welfare and Development Office (MSWDO) of Tagudin. It helps individuals and families address urgent needs during crisis situations.</p><p>Our staff will listen, assess your circumstances, and guide you through the appropriate assistance process.</p></div><div class="aid-grid observe"><article><span>⚕</span><h3>Medical</h3><p>Support for medicines, treatment, and medical needs.</p></article><article><span>⌂</span><h3>Food</h3><p>Food assistance for individuals and families in crisis.</p></article><article><span>✦</span><h3>Burial</h3><p>Assistance for families managing funeral expenses.</p></article><article><span>↗</span><h3>Transport & Education</h3><p>Help for urgent travel and school-related needs.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="public-section section-tint" id="avail"><div class="public-container"><div class="section-heading observe"><p class="public-kicker">HOW TO AVAIL</p><h2>Four simple steps</h2><p>Visit the MSWDO Tagudin office. Our personnel will help you understand what documents are needed for your situation.</p></div><ol class="steps"><li class="observe"><b>1</b><h3>Prepare your documents</h3><p>Bring a valid ID and documents related to your request, such as medical records or a barangay certificate.</p></li><li class="observe"><b>2</b><h3>Visit MSWDO Tagudin</h3><p>Go to the Municipal Social Welfare and Development Office during office hours.</p></li><li class="observe"><b>3</b><h3>Talk to a social worker</h3><p>Share your situation honestly so we can assess the appropriate assistance.</p></li><li class="observe"><b>4</b><h3>Receive guidance</h3><p>We will explain the next steps and keep you informed about your request.</p></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="public-section" id="eligibility"><div class="public-container two-col"><div class="section-intro observe"><p class="public-kicker">ELIGIBILITY & REQUIREMENTS</p><h2>What to bring</h2><p>Requirements may vary based on the type of assistance and your circumstances. Please bring original documents when possible.</p><a class="text-link" href="#contact">Ask MSWDO about your requirements →</a></div><div class="checklist observe"><h3>Common requirements</h3><ul><li>✓ Valid government-issued ID</li><li>✓ Barangay certificate of residency or indigency</li><li>✓ Documents supporting your request</li><li>✓ Medical certificate, prescription, or hospital bill for medical assistance</li><li>✓ Death certificate or funeral contract for burial assistance</li></ul><p>Assistance is subject to assessment and the availability of program funds.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="public-section section-tint" id="faqs"><div class="public-container faq-wrap"><div class="section-heading observe"><p class="public-kicker">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</p><h2>Questions we often receive</h2></div><div class="faq-list observe"><details><summary>Who can request AICS assistance?<span>+</span></summary><p>Residents of Tagudin who are experiencing a crisis situation may request an assessment. A social worker will review each request based on program guidelines.</p></details><details><summary>Is the assistance free?<span>+</span></summary><p>There is no fee for applying or being assessed for AICS assistance.</p></details><details><summary>How long does the assessment take?<span>+</span></summary><p>Processing time depends on the request, documents submitted, and the program's current procedures. Our staff will provide guidance during your visit.</p></details><details><summary>Can someone apply on behalf of a family member?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes, in many cases. Please bring identification and documents that explain your relationship to the person needing assistance.</p></details></div></div></section>
<section class="public-section" id="contact"><div class="public-container contact-panel observe"><div><p class="public-kicker">CONTACT & OFFICE LOCATION</p><h2>We are here to help.</h2><p>Visit or contact the MSWDO Tagudin office for questions about AICS assistance and the documents you need to prepare.</p></div><div class="contact-details"><p><b>⌖ MSWDO Tagudin</b><br>Municipal Hall, Tagudin, Ilocos Sur</p><p><b>◷ Office hours</b><br>Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–5:00 PM</p><p><b>✉ Email us</b><br><a href="mailto:mswdo@tagudin.gov.ph">mswdo@tagudin.gov.ph</a></p></div></div></section></main>
